From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: mediatek: read latched MT6878 measurements

The MT6878 LVTS controller only asserts the measurement valid bit when a
new conversion completes.  Requiring that bit for every thermal-zone read
makes userspace race the controller's 2.1 to 10.23 ms group interval and
causes intermittent -EAGAIN errors.

Follow the MT6878 vendor driver's read path for this generation: consume
the latched 16-bit measurement directly and reject zero until the first
conversion has completed.  Preserve the existing valid-bit polling for
all other LVTS implementations.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/thermal/mediatek/lvts_thermal.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/mediatek/lvts_thermal.c b/drivers/thermal/mediatek/lvts_thermal.c
index 0e3456c..a40e5a8 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/mediatek/lvts_thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/mediatek/lvts_thermal.c
@@ -335,8 +335,16 @@ static int lvts_get_temp(struct thermal_zone_device *tz, int *temp)
 	 * 16	: Valid temperature
 	 * 15-0	: Raw temperature
 	 */
-	rc = readl_poll_timeout(msr, value, value & BIT(16),
-				LVTS_MSR_READ_WAIT_US, LVTS_MSR_READ_TIMEOUT_US);
+	if (lvts_ctrl->lvts_data->mt6878_calibration) {
+		value = readl(msr);
+		if (!(value & 0xffff))
+			return -EAGAIN;
+		rc = 0;
+	} else {
+		rc = readl_poll_timeout(msr, value, value & BIT(16),
+					LVTS_MSR_READ_WAIT_US,
+					LVTS_MSR_READ_TIMEOUT_US);
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * As the thermal zone temperature will read before the
@@ -353,8 +361,6 @@ static int lvts_get_temp(struct thermal_zone_device *tz, int *temp)
 	 */
 	if (rc)
 		return -EAGAIN;
-	if (lvts_ctrl->lvts_data->mt6878_calibration && !(value & 0xffff))
-		return -EAGAIN;
 
 	*temp = lvts_raw_to_temp(lvts_ctrl, lvts_sensor, value & 0xFFFF);
 
